d/50571004/2026-college-football-week-13-top-25-betting-lines-odds","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Manuel to remain Michigan AD until new hire is found","description":"Warde Manuel has agreed to stay in the job as Michigan's athletic director until the school finds a new athletic director, sources told ESPN on Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-25T16:12:47.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50592920/sources-manuel-stay-job-new-michigan-ad-hired","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel and Dan Wetzel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Bottom 10 after Week 12: How the Bruins put the 'L' in UCLA","description":"While UCLA suffered its first loss, we still have a team looking for its first win -- and time is running out.","published":"2026-11-25T12:14:25.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50585901/bottom-10-week-12-ucla","type":"Story","byline":"Ryan McGee","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5197086/sahir-west","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sahir_West"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Sahir West","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sahir_West","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:28Z","intro":"Sahir West is an American college football defensive lineman for the UCLA Bruins. He previously played for the James Madison Dukes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"West attended Mount Saint Joseph High School in Baltimore, Maryland. As a junior, he totaled 63 tackles, ten sacks, and an interception. Following his high school career, West committed to play college football at James Madison University."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"West played sparingly in 2024, appearing in two games and earning a redshirt. His production increased the following season, recording ten tackles, 5.5 tackles for loss, and three sacks in the 2025 Sun Belt Conference Football Championship Game against Troy. At the conclusion of the regular season, West was named the Sun Belt Freshman of the Year and a first-team Freshman All-American by The Athletic."}]}}